# Components

1. Use Primevue components for all UI components.
2. Use `<script setup lang="ts">` for all components.

## Structure

Use the following layout for every component to keep imports and growth consistent:

```text
ComponentName/
  ├─ index.ts           # Re-export (single public entry)
  ├─ Container.vue      # Main component implementation
  ├─ useForm.ts         # Optional: composable when logic grows (e.g. forms)
  └─ DependentComponent.vue
```

ComponentName/index.ts
```ts
export { default as ComponentName } from "./Container.vue";
```

When a child piece becomes complex or needs its own hook, use the same pattern as the parent:

```text
ComponentName/
  └─ DependentComponent/
       ├─ index.ts
       └─ Container.vue
```

## State Rendering Pattern (for async data)

When a component displays data loaded asynchronously, add state sub-components:

```text
ComponentName/
  ├─ index.ts
  ├─ Container.vue      # Dispatches to Loading/Success/Failed
  ├─ Loading.vue        # Loading state (spinner, skeleton)
  ├─ Success.vue        # Success state (actual content)
  ├─ Failed.vue         # Error state (message, retry)
  └─ useXxx.ts          # Logic composable
```

Container.vue dispatches based on state type:
```vue
<template>
  <Loading v-if="state.type === 'Loading'" />
  <Failed v-else-if="state.type === 'Error'" :error="state.error" />
  <Success v-else-if="state.type === 'Success'" :data="state.data" />
  <InvalidState v-else />
</template>
```

## Data Flow

- Components get data from **services** (which compose stores + repositories).
- Components never call `sdk.backend.*` directly.
- Use `defineOptions({ name: "ComponentName" })` in Container.vue.
